      "content": "thanks for that. i'm just wondering though, does that mean the 'industry standard' is basically to let the risk of censorship override the right to political critique? it feels like if the standard is just to 'err on the side of caution' whenever a stereotype is involved, then satire becomes almost impossible to do without getting banned. wouldn't most policy experts argue that this actually undermines the purpose of satire by stripping away its edge?",
